  "notes": [
    "Both signals are 4K/60 RGB Full with incoming ALLM and Game Optimizer. Native settings scopes are sdrALLM/hdrALLM with Standard genre.",
    "SDR recalled brightness 80, Game Contrast 95 and adjustable-2.2 Gamma with fine offset 0. HDR recalled brightness 100, Game Contrast 100 and HGiG. Both used Game Color Depth 50, Game Sharpness 0, Game Black Level 50, stabilizers 10/10 and Fine Tune Dark Areas 0.",
    "Ordinary contrast/black-level/color/sharpness are disabled; the editor uses separate Game Optimizer values scoped by port, native range and genre.",
    "SDR Gamma offers high2 and mediumHavingLevel with a -3 through +3 fine adjustment. HDR Gamma and its fine adjustment are excluded, despite the native child flag remaining active.",
    "Expression Enhancer is enabled in PS5 HDR with off/detail/highlight choices, like Switch HDR and unlike the earlier PC HDR signals. Its saved Off value is preserved.",
    "Prevent Input Delay offers Standard/Boost (auto/on). HDMI 4 uses its saved Standard value, unlike HDMI 3 Boost. This was verified without changing the setting or claiming a measured latency benefit.",
    "Peak Brightness, Dynamic Contrast, both noise-reduction controls, Smooth Gradation, Real Cinema and TruMotion are natively disabled. Bridge 0.15.5 correctly withholds unsupported or unverified inactive processing controls; the inactive/active comparison found no falsely editable controls.",
    "Shared SDR game brightness covers PC, Nintendo and PS5 even under a narrow port filter. HDR brightness remains an independent input/preset standard. Port controls do not acquire format-specific storage in the editor.",
    "Neither sample includes hdmiVrrInfo; these are 60 Hz checks without reported VRR metadata. PS5 120 Hz and VRR-specific behavior remain unverified. QFT and DSC are off.",
    "The user temporarily disabled HDR and then restored it; the final capture confirms HDR10 gameplay. No TV picture setting was changed by the audit, saved standards and preferences are unchanged, and no temporary adjustments or pending restores remain.",
    "This audit verifies native scopes, values, ranges and availability. It does not measure displayed processing, latency or HDR calibration."
